   "t": "Мама просто завидует моему таланту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "Тогда давай играть дальше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я всегда готов играть с тобой.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now we'll go over it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Алиса, как тебе мой ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Alisa, how do you like my restaurant?' Welcoming his daughter, he proudly points to the ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ресторан",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", eager to hear her thoughts about his workplace.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "Пап, смотри, я похожа на тебя?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Dad, look, do I look like you?' Wondering about her appearance, the little girl asks if she is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "похожа",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to him, seeking some reassurance.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Конечно, солнышко!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course, sunshine!' A very sweet and common term of endearment is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "солнышко",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", translating literally as a little sun.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "У тебя мои глаза и улыбка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You have my eyes and smile.' Pointing out their shared facial features, he mentions her ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "улыбка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", matching the English expression for a smile.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "А мама говорит другое.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And mom says something else.' It turns out her mother has told her ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "другое",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", expressing a completely different opinion.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "Она говорит, слава богу, не похожа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She says, thank God, you do not look like him!' Repeating the harsh joke innocently, she shares what her mom ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "говорит",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", unaware of the insult.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это она так шутит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She was just joking.' Trying to save face, he claims she only ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "шутит",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " and does not mean it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не обращай внимания.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not pay any attention.' Wanting to change the subject, he asks his daughter not to give the insult any ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "внимания",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", moving the conversation forward.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "А ты тоже красивый, пап?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you handsome too, Dad?' Curious about his looks, she wonders if her father is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "красивый",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which means beautiful or good-looking.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я самый красивый повар в Москве!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am the most handsome chef in Moscow!' Full of confidence, the chef declares himself the best ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "повар",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " in the entire city.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "Но мама говорит, ты очень смешной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But mom says you are very funny.' According to her mother, his behavior is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "смешной",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which can mean laughable or amusing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мама просто завидует моему таланту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Mom is simply jealous of my talent.' Dismissing the insult, he replies that his ex-wife merely ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "завидует",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", feeling envious of his incredible skills.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "Тогда давай играть дальше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Then let us keep playing!' Eager to move on from the drama, she suggests they go ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "alisa",
   "t": "дальше",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", continuing their fun game together.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я всегда готов играть с тобой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am always ready to play with you.' Revealing his softer side, he promises he is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "всегда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
